  "scope": {
    "included": "Every named table and column in freshly migrated control.sqlite and <election_id>.sqlite, including SQLite-owned sqlite_sequence.",
    "excluded": "This bounded registry does not enumerate arbitrary nested JSON properties, in-memory state, client/trustee stores, file-only artifacts or unimplemented specification tables.",
    "enforcement": "packages/server/test/data-inventory.test.ts compares this reviewed inventory with real migrated databases using SQLite schema introspection.",
    "limitations": [
      "This analyzes existing storage; it adds no access-control, encryption, deletion or retention guarantee.",
      "Classes are the C0-C4 definitions in QV-06. QV-28's separate P0-P4 taxonomy is evidence, not an interchangeable set of class names.",
      "C3 conservatively covers private operational containers by the D24/D25 precedent. It does not imply every field is credential material or encrypted.",
      "C0 describes public election content and derived values, not a promise that every local cache/index row is immutable or permanent. Read-key access can restrict election readers.",
      "A container class covers the whole column. Its rationale documents mixed content, without validating arbitrary future JSON fields or future writers.",
      "C4 means memory-only and cannot classify a persisted column. Signed-request replay nonces are distinct from the D26 session/CSRF model.",
      "No retention periods are copied here: QV-06's target schedule and current storage behavior are separate questions."
    ]
  },
